Z||000008||Pretender||06-12-99||11:07 PM||||i think it was an '91 CRX., i wouldn't doubt that the iceman flows cooler air it's just that the sizing of the tube is hold it back from the power...i'm not sure if you(anyone) under stood what i wrote about the air-flow., so i'll try again....imagine a 2 inch tube., on top of that a 4 inch tube funnled., now try forcing water down the 4 inch tube into the 2"., it will back up., if you would remove the 4" funnel and only forced(same pressure as before) a 2" stream down the tube it would never back up....it's all about flow. The flow is more important then the temp, if iceman would equal out their flow design i would have no doubt that they would have the best on the market., untill the new carbon fiber ones come out that is...i read in another mag. that C-F is 200 degrees more resistant to heat then alum...i'm not sure what the temp to horsepower ratio is but i seen it somewhere on this board....:o)
