Z||000010||theogre||06-13-99||11:20 AM||||proper flow is allot of the problem but air density, which is affected by temp and moisture content, does have a major power to change performance. The same volume of air at diferant density will use diferant amounts of fuel. Air that is more dense will have a higher compression as well.
Z||000011||lowCG||06-14-99||01:16 AM||||Intake runners are merely collumns of air that resonate at level that is what a motor will require.Volume is a major factor as well,and if more is needed sometimes a tapered or cone works better,there are many performance engines that use this.The cone will make for a more dense charge,if the motor and air/fuel mixture aren't ready to accomodate this,it may not respond,and will have run better without.
